	cmd := &cobra.Command{
		Use:   "schema",
		Short: "Define property fields shared by sibling or child pages.",
		Long:  "# Manage shared field definitions\n\nA property **schema** defines the fields shared by sibling Library\npages: their names, types, and sort directions. The pages hold their own\nvalues. For example, a directory can define `status` as text and\n`priority` as a number for its entries.\n\nThe command's target matters: selecting a parent addresses the schema\nfor its children; selecting a child addresses the schema it shares with\nits siblings. This is a group-wide structure change, rather than a value\nchange on one page.\n\n## Commands and workflows\n\nA page's property schema is shared with its siblings. `get PARENT` reads\nthe child-property schema on a parent; `children PARENT` updates it.\n`set CHILD` updates the schema of the selected child and its siblings.\nThese are different scopes: inspect the hierarchy first.\n\nUse `properties set` for values on one page. Schema changes define\nnames, types, and sort directions across a group of pages.\n\n## Examples\n\n~~~sh\nsd page properties schema get docs --output json\n~~~\n",
		Args:  groupArgs,
		RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
			return cmd.Help()
		},
	}
